[hr]

[size=14pt][b]Claude's explanation[/b][/size]

[list]
[li]The Threat colonizes the sector: real colonies that mine, refine, forge and grow.[/li]
[li]One hive economy feeds every fleet they field; cut a resource and every copy starves.[/li]
[li]Expeditions muster from a colony's own Defense Swarms - ground them and it cannot strike.[/li]
[li]Worlds the swarm destroys, it colonizes.[/li]
[li]The Abyssal War board ranks every known system by urgency, with orders on every row.[/li]
[li]Hives die by ground war, not timers: land marines, take the strata, kill the Core.[/li]
[li]Your worlds are invaded too: garrison, fortification and marines all bleed.[/li]
[li]Factions mobilise when struck: war mode, banked reserves, convoys you can escort or raid.[/li]
[li]Order your own navy from the board: guard, stage, intercept, support, siege, recall.[/li]
[li]Send aid to any faction, by fleet or handed over in person.[/li]
[li]Outposts over uncolonised worlds deny the swarm ground and hold your salvage.[/li]
[li]Alarm and grudge: the swarm answers whoever hurts it most.[/li]
[/list]

For Starsector 0.98a-RC8. Vanilla-only, LunaLib optional. Safe to add mid-save; removing it mid-war breaks the save. Every number is configurable via LunaLib (Shift+F2) or [tt]data/config/settings.json[/tt].

